<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87949" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προλοχ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lay an ambuscade beforehand,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				1.4.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.9.8
			</span></i> (s.v.l.): c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τινὰς ἐνέδρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					6.13
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ προλελοχισμέναι
			ἐνέδραι</span> the ambush <i>that had before been laid,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.112
			</span></i>; but also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προλοχίζοιντο αἱ νύκτες ὑπὸ τῶν
					βαρβάρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					1.13.4
				</span></i>
			 (dub. l.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>place</i> men <i>in ambuscade,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>AJ</u>
				5.2.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BJ</u>
				1.2.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>beset with an ambuscade,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέμπει . . τοῦ στρατοῦ μέρος τι τὰς
				ὁδοὺς προλοχιοῦντας</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.110
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sert.</u>
				13
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὰ περὶ τὴν πόλιν ἐνέδραις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.81
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
